+Add a local Mirror preview toggle to the wardrobe so the player can examine asymmetric clothes and the existing movement previews from the other facing direction. Flip one enclosing SVG group around the 200px view box; preserve the sampled art, pose, finite clock and deadline, equipped items, saved data and grid identity. Mirror only the local preview and reset on remount; keep the choice through pose, outfit, movement and reduced-motion changes. It remains usable under reduced motion because it makes one immediate view change without a transition or a new clock.
+
+Use a 48px icon button with a stable accessible name (Mirror preview of the pet), aria-pressed, a visible focus ring and a native title. Put it in the stage's upper-right empty corner rather than adding a control row or reducing art height. Retain the five movement controls and existing Show preview ordering. The icon is two outward arrows around a dashed vertical axis. Append mirrored preview to the image description only when flipped. Check real character-ink/control clearance at every layout; if the proposed corner overlaps visible art, revise the arrangement before acceptance.
+
+Before product edits, verify failing unit/native tests. Test all species and poses, each finite movement deadline, toggling twice, stable art/grid, no save, outfit updates, hidden expiry and live system/device reduction. Native tests inspect actual inverse SVG matrices, positive/negative determinant and mirror involution, visible/keyboard/touch target geometry, focus ring, saved tables, the same art node and original Rest expiry. Review 320/390/640/844/1280 widths at 100/200 percent root text and dressed species stills. One low-priority resource-guarded job/worker/browser at a time; use a higher launch reserve for the full suite following Batch49's 2.2GB sampled minimum.
+
+Batch49 review passed and checkpoint f5b26cf is saved. This batch starts from that checkpoint. No external publication or persistent schema setting.
+
+The initial Head tab revealed an existing short-phone layout defect: its taller item grid left only 32.40625px for the preview at 320x568, whereas prior layout fixtures ended on the shorter On back tab. Retain that baseline capture and failing 90px regression. Reduce the existing short-phone panel cap from 180px to 120px so item rows remain scrollable and the character keeps over 90px; enlarged-text flowing layouts retain their uncapped panels. Keep the initial mirror prototype failures, probe and source snapshots distinct from final acceptance. Device preference assertions wait for the actual disabled Rest DOM before scheduler inspection.
+
+Final item-panel policy preserves the existing global flow thresholds. The side panel establishes its own inline-size container; panels at most 16rem wrap categories and use two item columns. Five wide-screen categories form 3+2 rows; six phone tabs retain two columns. Category tabs remain sticky inside their existing scroll panel. Native image review exposed the landscape tab strip after focusing the mirror and 200-percent gift-label overlap; the initial 640px sidebar guard passed, while the 1280px enlarged gift-bound guard failed before this correction.
+
+Movement clearance retains strict nonintersecting body/accent rectangles for static layouts and the held Rest capture. Rotated Bun Hop bounds include empty corners: preserve the diagnostic image and failed rectangular probe. For moving poses, native painted-geometry hit tests inspect any intersecting rectangle at 1px intervals, with temporary pointer-event changes restored to exact inline styles; zero samples may hit character or active accent ink. This is sampled native geometry, not exhaustive pixel/temporal certification. All five movements at .25/.5/.75 in both directions give 90 configurations across three species.
